              "authors": "Allen R; Rad-Men\u00e9ndez C; Green DH; Campbell CN; De Boever F; Field J; MacKechnie K; Ross M; Saxon R; Thomas N; Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa collective; University of Oxford and Wytham Woods Genome Acquisition Lab; Earlham Institute Genome Acquisition Lab and Protists Project; Darwin Tree of Life Barcoding collective; Wellcome Sanger Institute Tree of Life Management, Samples and Laboratory team; Wellcome Sanger Institute Scientific Operations: Sequencing Operations; Wellcome Sanger Institute Tree of Life Core Informatics team; Tree of Life Core Informatics collective; Darwin Tree of Life Consortium",
              "year": 2024,
              "notes": "source_type=journal_article; discovery_mode=cross_reference; accessed_on=2026-10-14; source_url=https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11833223/fullTextXML; raw_archive=references_cache/papers/primary_xml/marvania-PMC11833223-algal-followup-20261014.xml; markdown_archive=references_cache/papers/primary_xml/marvania-PMC11833223-algal-followup-20261014.md; access_scope=Full JATS article, version 1; bounded cultivation methods. PMID:39967591; PMCID:PMC11833223. Publication year is 2024; the title-ending 2004 is taxonomic authority context, not publication year. Ten individual and nine collective authors agree between PubMed XML and JATS. Archived PubMed/JATS notice lists checked; no exhaustive notice search claimed. locator=Methods / Sample acquisition and nucleic acid extraction; exact excerpt=\"M. coccoides CCAP 251/1B was cultivated in EG:JM medium\". reported scientific name=Marvania coccoides; strain=CCAP 251/1B; accepted study name=Marvania coccoides; canonical scientific name=Marvania coccoides; NCBITaxon:133487; actual rank=species; taxonomy_match=exact_name_at_species_rank; lookup_url=https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Browser/wwwtax.cgi?id=133487; lookup_date=2026-10-14; Species scientific name and rank verified; exact full strain-name query returned no hit and does not prove absence or an exact strain taxon. The study reports cultivation at 20 degrees C and a 12:12 h light:dark period. The printed light intensity has m^-1 s^-1 units; it is not silently corrected to area-based irradiance. No ingredient differences are stated, so no variant is invented. The study cites Jaworski 1981 and Schlosser 1982 but does not restate the complete formula. Current CCAP EG:JM specifies a 1:1 mixture; this is not proof of the historical study formulation or every flattened stock amount. No new target organism or growth metric is attached while full formula and physical-state equivalence remain unresolved. The scientific-name taxonomy paragraph uses the species ID in an abbreviated taxonomic list; the actual NCBI rank is species. Taxonomy source=references_cache/papers/taxonomy/algal-followup-next-20261014.xml. This owner is encoded SOLID_AGAR; the paper does not support that agar formulation. "
            }
